@flexiarg operator/bare-continue-nudge
@title The Bare Continue Nudge
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-lQwNl8 turn-qa25CU
@parent orchestration/state-in-substrate-deltas-in-messages
@context A long-running agent session where the shared record (transcript, substrate, mission doc) already holds the task state.

! conclusion: Send the minimal continuation signal ('Let's continue') and let the agent recover context from the record; treat it as a pure delta on shared state.

  + IF:
    The operator wants work to resume or proceed and has nothing new to add — no new constraint, object, or success criterion.

  + HOWEVER:
    The message carries zero content; it only works because state lives in the shared substrate and the agent can recover what 'continue' means. Where state lives in the message channel, a bare continue is unanswerable.

  + THEN:
    Send the minimal continuation signal ('Let's continue') and let the agent recover context from the record; treat it as a pure delta on shared state.

  + BECAUSE:
    The bare continue is the degenerate case of that pattern: a message that is nothing but a delta, viable precisely because the substrate holds the state it modifies.
